{{!
    @template core/form_autocomplete_selection

    Moodle template for the wrapper of currently selected items in an autocomplate form element.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * multiple True if this field allows multiple selections
    * selectionId The dom id of the current selection list.
    * items List of items with label and value fields (used by the partial).
    * noSelectionString String to use when no items are selected (used by the partial).

    Note: this template is always rendered with an empty "items" list (the real, current
    selection is populated afterwards by JS). The "listbox" ARIA semantics (role,
    aria-labelledby, tabindex, aria-required, aria-multiselectable) are therefore only ever
    meaningful once there are items, so they are added/removed by
    updateSelectionRegionAccessibility() in core/form-autocomplete instead of being hardcoded
    here - a listbox role must not be exposed while it has no valid option/group children.

    Example context (json):
    { "multiple": true, "selectionId": 1, "items": [
        { "label": "Item label with <strong>tags</strong>", "value": "5" },
        { "label": "Another item label with <strong>tags</strong>", "value": "4" }
    ], "noSelectionString": "No selection" }
}}
<span class="visually-hidden" id="{{selectionId}}-label">{{#str}}selecteditems, form{{/str}}</span>
<span class="visually-hidden" id="{{selectionId}}-remove-description">{{#str}}pressentertoremove, form{{/str}}</span>
<div id="{{selectionId}}-announcer" aria-live="polite" role="status" class="visually-hidden"></div>
<div{{!
    }} class="form-autocomplete-selection w-100 {{#multiple}}form-autocomplete-multiple{{/multiple}}"{{!
    }} id="{{selectionId}}"{{!
    }} aria-atomic="true">
    {{> core/form_autocomplete_selection_items }}
</div>
